WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:24.000
Forces and motion. Notice what changes and what stays the same.

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:31.000
LEARNING TARGET: Relate net force, mass and acceleration

00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:38.000
THE BIG IDEA: Newton’s second law relates net force, mass and acceleration for a defined system in an inertial frame.

00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:45.000
WORKED EXAMPLE: Illustrative 1,200 kg × 2 m/s² = 2,400 N net force, before road loads and traction limits.

00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:52.000
PAUSE AND PREDICT: Free-body diagram

00:00:52.000 --> 00:00:59.000
MODEL LIMIT: A system diagram is a model, not a finished vehicle or proof of roadworthiness.

00:00:59.000 --> 00:01:06.000
TAKEAWAY: Relate net force, mass and acceleration
